---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../data/site';
---

<DocsLayout title="How It Works" sectionLabel="How It Works" activeSlug="architecture">

  <section class="section">
    <h2>How VibeCrew Works</h2>
    <p>VibeCrew is a system of interlocking parts: a plugin shell, specialized agents, lifecycle hooks, slash commands, bash scripts, per-project runtime state, and a live status line that surfaces it all at a glance. Each piece solves a specific problem that emerges when AI builds software autonomously.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Problems Solved (tabs) ── -->
  <section class="section">
    <h3>Seven Problems VibeCrew Solves</h3>
    <div class="problem-tabs">
      <div class="problem-tab-bar" role="tablist">
        <button class="problem-tab-btn active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab="rule-drift">Rule Drift</button>
        <button class="problem-tab-btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="context-bloat">Context Bloat</button>
        <button class="problem-tab-btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="session-amnesia">Session Amnesia</button>
        <button class="problem-tab-btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="workflow-errors">Workflow Errors</button>
        <button class="problem-tab-btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="quality-decay">Quality Decay</button>
        <button class="problem-tab-btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="ad-hoc-decisions">Ad-Hoc Decisions</button>
        <button class="problem-tab-btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="split-attention">Split Attention</button>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-tab-panel active" data-panel="rule-drift">
        <span class="problem-label red">Problem</span>
        <h4 class="problem-headline">AI forgets rules mid-session</h4>
        <p class="problem-desc">Large language models don't reliably follow instructions embedded in long contexts. The more code and conversation accumulates, the more likely the model is to ignore project conventions, skip required steps, or write code before the architecture is decided.</p>
        <div class="solution-box">
          <p class="solution-box-title">How VibeCrew solves this</p>
          <table class="solution-table">
            <tr><td>Phase gate hook</td><td>A bash script intercepts every file write. If foundation artifacts (VISION.md, TDR, architecture diagrams) aren't complete, the write is blocked before the model even sees the result.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Quality gate hook</td><td>After every task completion, typecheck, lint, and build run automatically. Failures are caught instantly, not deferred to a later review.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Path restriction hook</td><td>Writes outside the project root are blocked, preventing accidental modifications to system files or other projects.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Zero token cost</td><td>All enforcement runs as bash scripts in lifecycle hooks. No tokens are spent reminding the model of rules &mdash; they're enforced deterministically.</td></tr>
          </table>
          <a class="solution-link" href={url('/hooks.html')}>View hook system &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-tab-panel" data-panel="context-bloat">
        <span class="problem-label red">Problem</span>
        <h4 class="problem-headline">Context windows fill up fast</h4>
        <p class="problem-desc">Research tasks &mdash; reading documentation, evaluating libraries, analyzing codebases &mdash; consume thousands of tokens. Once the context window fills, the model loses earlier instructions and code, forcing expensive restarts.</p>
        <div class="solution-box">
          <p class="solution-box-title">How VibeCrew solves this</p>
          <table class="solution-table">
            <tr><td>Worktree isolation</td><td>Expensive agents (Stack Scout, Builder, Code Reviewer) run in separate git worktrees with their own context windows. Only their distilled output re-enters the main session.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>MCP servers</td><td>Context7 serves library documentation on demand. Chrome DevTools inspects live pages. No need to paste large blocks of reference material.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Forced compaction</td><td>During <code>/run-backlog</code>, the system forces <code>/compact</code> between features, preventing context rot across long autonomous runs.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Context warnings</td><td>A Stop hook monitors usage and warns at 45% and 60%, giving you time to wrap up before hitting the limit.</td></tr>
          </table>
          <a class="solution-link" href={url('/agents.html')}>View agent topology &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-tab-panel" data-panel="session-amnesia">
        <span class="problem-label red">Problem</span>
        <h4 class="problem-headline">No persistent memory across sessions</h4>
        <p class="problem-desc">Each Claude Code session starts with a blank slate. Without external state, the AI can't know which features are done, what phase you're in, what decisions were made, or what quality trends look like over time.</p>
        <div class="solution-box">
          <p class="solution-box-title">How VibeCrew solves this</p>
          <table class="solution-table">
            <tr><td><code>.vibecrew/state.json</code></td><td>Tracks foundation completion status, the active feature, and current phase. Every session starts by reading this file to resume exactly where you left off.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Backlog &amp; signals</td><td>Feature specs live in <code>backlog.json</code>. Inter-agent signals coordinate handoffs between agents working in parallel.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Session logs &amp; scores</td><td>Every session is logged with its Vibe Score breakdown. The Performance Coach reads score history to detect patterns across multiple sessions.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Handoff documents</td><td>When context runs low, <code>/handoff</code> generates a structured document capturing all in-progress work, decisions, and next steps for the next session.</td></tr>
          </table>
          <a class="solution-link" href={url('/runtime.html')}>View state structure &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-tab-panel" data-panel="workflow-errors">
        <span class="problem-label red">Problem</span>
        <h4 class="problem-headline">Manual workflows are error-prone</h4>
        <p class="problem-desc">Remembering to run tests, update docs, check accessibility, format code, and write a changelog entry after every feature is tedious. Steps get skipped, especially during long sessions or when working under pressure.</p>
        <div class="solution-box">
          <p class="solution-box-title">How VibeCrew solves this</p>
          <table class="solution-table">
            <tr><td>Slash commands</td><td><code>/wrap</code> runs quality checks, generates docs, updates the changelog, computes the Vibe Score, and commits &mdash; in a single trigger.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>/run-backlog</code></td><td>Plans, builds, tests, reviews, and documents every feature in the backlog sequentially, with automatic compaction between features.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Auto-formatting hook</td><td>Every file write triggers Prettier/formatter automatically. Code style is never a manual step.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Slash commands</td><td>Cover the full lifecycle &mdash; from <code>/setup</code> and <code>/plan-features</code> through <code>/tdd</code>, <code>/review</code>, <code>/e2e</code>, <code>/a11y</code>, to <code>/release</code>.</td></tr>
          </table>
          <a class="solution-link" href={url('/command-flow.html')}>View command reference &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-tab-panel" data-panel="quality-decay">
        <span class="problem-label red">Problem</span>
        <h4 class="problem-headline">Quality degrades without oversight</h4>
        <p class="problem-desc">AI-generated code tends to accumulate dead code, unnecessary abstractions, and subtle regressions over time. Without continuous feedback, each session makes the codebase slightly worse &mdash; and nobody notices until it's a mess.</p>
        <div class="solution-box">
          <p class="solution-box-title">How VibeCrew solves this</p>
          <table class="solution-table">
            <tr><td>Vibe Score</td><td>A quantitative quality metric computed every session. Starts at 100, applies deductions for prompt churn, tool loops, missing tests, skipped reviews, and documentation drift. Bonuses for TDD, clean sessions, and full coverage.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Performance Coach</td><td>Analyzes score trends across sessions. When anti-patterns recur 3+ times, it proposes permanent CLAUDE.md rule mutations &mdash; creating a self-improving feedback loop.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Code Reviewer</td><td>Read-only review against the feature spec, TDR compliance, and project conventions. Catches architectural drift before it ships.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Code Simplifier</td><td>Detects dead code, flattens unnecessary abstractions, and reduces API surface area. Runs on demand via <code>/simplify</code>.</td></tr>
          </table>
          <a class="solution-link" href={url('/self-improving.html')}>View feedback loop &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-tab-panel" data-panel="ad-hoc-decisions">
        <span class="problem-label red">Problem</span>
        <h4 class="problem-headline">Architecture decisions are ad-hoc</h4>
        <p class="problem-desc">Without a structured research phase, AI picks whatever framework or pattern it saw most in training data. Technology choices are made implicitly during coding rather than explicitly during planning &mdash; leading to inconsistent stacks and regretted decisions.</p>
        <div class="solution-box">
          <p class="solution-box-title">How VibeCrew solves this</p>
          <table class="solution-table">
            <tr><td>Two-tier workflow</td><td>Tier 1 (foundation) must complete before any source code is written. This includes VISION.md, design system, TDR, and architecture diagrams &mdash; enforced by the phase gate hook.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Stack Scout agent</td><td>A dedicated research agent that evaluates technologies in an isolated worktree, produces a structured Technology Decision Record (TDR), and never writes application code.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Opponent Processor</td><td>A devil's advocate agent that stress-tests TDR decisions with debate matrices and risk assessments before development begins.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Architecture diagrams</td><td>Five Mermaid diagrams (system topology, schema, state flows, API sequences, component tree) are generated during Tier 1 and referenced by every agent.</td></tr>
          </table>
          <a class="solution-link" href={url('/architecture.html')}>View two-tier workflow &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-tab-panel" data-panel="split-attention">
        <span class="problem-label red">Problem</span>
        <h4 class="problem-headline">You have to babysit every session</h4>
        <p class="problem-desc">Without automation, you're glued to the terminal &mdash; reading every output, deciding when to intervene, and context-switching constantly. Running multiple projects in parallel is impossible because each session demands your continuous attention.</p>
        <div class="solution-box">
          <p class="solution-box-title">How VibeCrew solves this</p>
          <table class="solution-table">
            <tr><td>Interrupt-only notifications</td><td>The system stays silent during normal operation and only pings you on three conditions: permission stalls, task completion, and critical failures. No noise, no polling.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Warp deep-linking</td><td>Notifications include <code>warp://session/&lt;id&gt;</code> URIs that jump you straight to the terminal tab that needs attention &mdash; no hunting through tabs.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Autonomous feature builds</td><td><code>/run-backlog</code> processes the entire feature queue autonomously &mdash; planning, building, testing, reviewing, and documenting each feature without manual triggers between steps.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Multi-project parallel work</td><td>Combined with per-project state (<code>.vibecrew/</code>), you can run VibeCrew across several projects simultaneously, responding only when notified.</td></tr>
          </table>
          <a class="solution-link" href={url('/warp.html')}>View Warp integration &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── Status Line ── -->
  <section class="section">
    <h3>The Status Line</h3>
    <p>While VibeCrew runs, a persistent status line at the bottom of your Claude Code terminal shows real-time session state &mdash; model, context usage, cost, active feature and phase, Vibe Score, and compaction count. It updates after every assistant message at zero token cost.</p>

    <pre class="status-line-mock"><code>Opus 4.6 <span class="sl-ctx-green">▓▓▓▓░░░░░░ 38%</span> | <span class="sl-cost">$0.42</span> | <span class="sl-feat">auth-flow · Code</span> | <span class="sl-score">↑85+</span> | <span class="sl-dur">12m</span> | <span class="sl-compact">⟳0</span></code></pre>

    <p><a href={url('/status-line.html')}>View full status line documentation &rarr;</a></p>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── Page Grid ── -->
  <section class="section">
    <h3>Explore the System</h3>
    <div class="page-grid">
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/status-line.html')}>
        <h3>Status Line</h3>
        <p>The persistent status bar: model, context usage, cost, feature, Vibe Score, and compaction count.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View status line &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/plugin.html')}>
        <h3>Plugin Structure</h3>
        <p>The manifest, MCP servers, permissions, hooks, scripts, agents, and skills that make up the plugin.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View plugin anatomy &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/agents.html')}>
        <h3>Sub-Agents</h3>
        <p>Specialized AI agents with scoped tool access, model selection, and worktree isolation.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View agent topology &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/hooks.html')}>
        <h3>Hooks</h3>
        <p>Lifecycle hooks that enforce safety, quality, and workflow rules at zero token cost.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View hook system &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/mcp-servers.html')}>
        <h3>MCP Servers</h3>
        <p>Bundled + registry servers activated on demand once the project architecture is clear.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View MCP integration &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/command-flow.html')}>
        <h3>Slash Commands</h3>
        <p>Commands across setup, planning, development, quality, safety, and session management.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View command reference &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/skills.html')}>
        <h3>Skills Reference</h3>
        <p>Every SKILL.md file with category filters &mdash; from zero-cost scripts to multi-agent orchestrations.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">Browse all skills &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/scripts.html')}>
        <h3>Bash Scripts</h3>
        <p>Deterministic scripts that handle state mutations, scoring, git operations, and formatting.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View script catalog &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/templates.html')}>
        <h3>Templates</h3>
        <p>Scaffolding blueprints for foundation docs, state files, test configs, CI/CD, and reporting.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View template catalog &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/runtime.html')}>
        <h3>Runtime State</h3>
        <p>The <code>.vibecrew/</code> directory: JSON state files, session logs, scores, signals, and handoffs.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View state structure &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/safety.html')}>
        <h3>Permissions &amp; Safety</h3>
        <p>Three-layer defense: permission rules, hook guards, and quality gates.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View safety model &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/self-improving.html')}>
        <h3>Self-Improving System</h3>
        <p>Performance Coach, CLAUDE.md mutations, Vibe Score, and cross-project telemetry.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View feedback loop &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/personalization.html')}>
        <h3>Personalization</h3>
        <p>User profiles with adaptive agent behavior &mdash; every agent adjusts to your experience level, working style, and preferences.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View personalization &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/gamification.html')}>
        <h3>Gamification &amp; Vibe Score</h3>
        <p>Vibe Score quality metrics, XP, leveling, badges, skill tree, streaks, challenges, and quizzes that reward good development habits.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View gamification &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href={url('/dashboard.html')}>
        <h3>Vibe Dashboard</h3>
        <p>Browser-based VitePress dashboard with Kanban board, trends, achievements, and settings.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View dashboard guide &rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</DocsLayout>

<script is:inline>
  // Problem tabs
  (function() {
    var bar = document.querySelector('.problem-tab-bar');
    if (!bar) return;
    bar.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
      var btn = e.target.closest('.problem-tab-btn');
      if (!btn) return;
      var tab = btn.getAttribute('data-tab');
      bar.querySelectorAll('.problem-tab-btn').forEach(function(b) {
        b.classList.remove('active');
        b.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'false');
      });
      btn.classList.add('active');
      btn.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'true');
      document.querySelectorAll('.problem-tab-panel').forEach(function(p) {
        p.classList.toggle('active', p.getAttribute('data-panel') === tab);
      });
    });
  })();

  // Backward-compat: redirect old hash-based tab URLs to new pages
  (function() {
    var map = {
      '#plugin': 'plugin.html',
      '#agents': 'agents.html',
      '#hooks': 'hooks.html',
      '#commands': 'command-flow.html',
      '#skills': 'skills.html',
      '#scripts': 'scripts.html',
      '#runtime': 'runtime.html',
      '#safety': 'safety.html',
      '#dashboard': 'dashboard.html',
    };
    var hash = window.location.hash;
    if (hash && map[hash]) {
      window.location.replace(map[hash]);
    }
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .status-line-mock {
    background: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: .85rem 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    position: relative;
  }
  .status-line-mock::before {
    content: 'STATUS LINE';
    position: absolute;
    top: .45rem;
    right: .75rem;
    font-size: .6rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }
  .status-line-mock code {
    background: none;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: .9rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-text);
    white-space: nowrap;
    line-height: 2;
  }
  .sl-ctx-green { color: var(--color-green); }
  .sl-ctx-yellow { color: var(--color-amber); }
  .sl-ctx-red { color: var(--color-red); }
  .sl-cost { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .sl-feat { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .sl-score { color: var(--color-green); }
  .sl-dur { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .sl-compact { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .status-line-table th {
    font-size: .78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .03em;
    padding: .6rem .75rem;
  }
  .status-line-table td {
    font-size: .84rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding: .6rem .75rem;
  }
  .status-line-table td:first-child {
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    width: 130px;
  }
  .status-line-table td:nth-child(2) {
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .82rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    width: 160px;
  }
  .status-line-table td:nth-child(2) code {
    font-size: .82rem;
  }
</style>
